      "id": "I_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABNPYQSA",
      "title": "replace flashblocks spec with subblocks spec",
      "author": "geoknee",
      "number": 929,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "body": "We should only the public facing parts of subblocks. See the docs here:\n\nhttps://docs.optimism.io/op-stack/features/subblocks\nhttps://docs.optimism.io/app-developers/guides/transactions/subblocks-and-gas-usage\n\n\nFor example we should sate the state root doesn't need to be / isn't populated. And cover the wire format and JSON-RPC. It can be very lightweight.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-18T15:29:20Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABNna8dw",
      "title": "interop: expiry-boundary restatements are one second stricter than the normative Message Expiry Invariant",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 931,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "body": "The interop message-expiry boundary is stated three times across the interop specs, and the two summary restatements disagree with the normative definition by one second. Both production implementations follow the normative definition.\n\n## Normative definition\n\n[`specs/interop/messaging.md` § Message Expiry Invariant](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/blob/2049036afe878a7cb443f513f4e6ca453d90c340/specs/interop/messaging.md?plain=1#L153-L163):\n\n> The expiry invariant invalidates inclusion of any executing message with\n> `id.timestamp + EXPIRY_TIME < executing_block.timestamp`\n\n⇒ a message executed **exactly at** `id.timestamp + EXPIRY_TIME` is **valid**.\n\n## Drifted restatement 1 — same file\n\n[`messaging.md` invariants summary list](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/blob/2049036afe878a7cb443f513f4e6ca453d90c340/specs/interop/messaging.md?plain=1#L127-L128):\n\n> [Message Expiry Invariant]: The timestamp at the time of inclusion of the executing message MUST be **lower than** the initiating message timestamp (as defined in the [`Identifier`]) + `EXPIRY_TIME`.\n\n`exec < init + EXPIRY_TIME` ⇒ the boundary case is **invalid**. Should read \"lower than **or equal to**\".\n\n## Drifted restatement 2 — derivation.md\n\n[`specs/interop/derivation.md`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/blob/2049036afe878a7cb443f513f4e6ca453d90c340/specs/interop/derivation.md?plain=1#L34-L37):\n\n> - `t > execution_timestamp - expiry_window`, where `expiry_window` is the expiry window in seconds.\n\nAt the boundary, `t > execution_timestamp - expiry_window` is `init > init` = false ⇒ **invalid**. Should be `t >= execution_timestamp - expiry_window` (validity `exec <= init + window` ⇔ `t >= execution_timestamp - expiry_window`).\n\n## Implementations follow the normative definition\n\nBoth consensus implementations accept the boundary case (`exec == init + EXPIRY_TIME`):\n\n- op-supernode: [`op-supernode/supernode/activity/interop/algo.go#L192`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/9e4981ed41d69cbb1a03f0af7d64d5e070d59e21/op-supernode/supernode/activity/interop/algo.go#L192) — rejects only on `execMsg.Timestamp + messageExpiryWindow < executingTimestamp`.\n- kona: [`rust/kona/crates/protocol/interop/src/graph.rs#L406`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/9e4981ed41d69cbb1a03f0af7d64d5e070d59e21/rust/kona/crates/protocol/interop/src/graph.rs#L406) — rejects only on `init < exec.saturating_sub(window)`.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAlign both restatements to the normative § Message Expiry Invariant (they are summaries, the normative text and both implementations already agree): \"lower than or equal to\" in the messaging.md bullet, and `>=` in the derivation.md bullet.\n\n🤖 *Co-created with Claude (Fable 5)*\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-20T23:13:17Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-08-21T14:12:09Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 0
    }
  ],
  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABAK3jGA",
      "title": "pcd: align specs with the shipped deployment pipeline",
      "author": "0xiamflux",
      "number": 930,
      "body": "## Context\r\nThe PCD spec pages landed before super root support and the `prepare` / `prestate` /\r\n`continue` hardening merged. This updates all three against the code that shipped. Spec-only.\r\n\r\n- Both game families are deployable at genesis. New definitions for Super Root, Starting Anchor\r\n  Root, Selected Prestate and Fallback Prestate replace `Prestate / Prestate Hash`, and\r\n  `iOPD-002` pins the root and its `l2SequenceNumber` per family.\r\n- OPCM's game-type check is scoped to the `SUPER_ROOT_GAMES_MIGRATION` mode, plus the three\r\n  value checks PCD added: non-zero anchor root, no `0xdead` placeholder, non-zero prestate.\r\n- `DeployOPChainInput` gains `startingAnchorRoot` and `cannonAbsolutePrestate`. A permissionless\r\n  deploy enables the respected game and its guardian fallback.\r\n- Command behavior now matches the pipeline: anchor pinning, prestate invalidation on every\r\n  `prepare`, and `continue`'s digest, fork-simulation, anchor and post-deploy checks.\r\n- The `BLOCKHASH` and second-RPC guards never shipped and are replaced by what the code does.\r\n\r\nClaims verified against `615b1c75dd` and `9714d4dd2c` on `develop` and op-deployer's three\r\ncommands.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-18T16:09:12Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 331,
      "deletions": 118
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABAjzvdQ",
      "title": "specs: replace flashblocks with subblocks",
      "author": "bitwiseguy",
      "number": 933,
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Replace the detailed Flashblocks specification with a minimal, consumer-facing Subblocks specification.\n- Document the WebSocket payload format, sequencing guarantees, JSON-RPC behavior, and transaction inclusion implications.\n- Clarify that Subblocks are a backwards-compatible successor to Flashblocks, except that `state_root`, `block_hash`, `withdrawals_root`, and `withdrawals` are zeroed.\n- Update the specs book summary and spelling dictionary.\n\n## Related Issues\n* Closes https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/issues/929",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T14:09:14Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 190,
      "deletions": 1398
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc7-fls8",
      "title": "holocene: require span batch overlap checks",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 928,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nRequire Holocene span batches to retain Delta's overlap checks before streaming singular batches. Clarify that only the remaining full span-batch checks are deferred.\n\nImplementation: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/22215\n\n## Safety\n\nThis is a retroactive protocol change. It is expected to be safe because no production chain is known to have posted a span batch whose overlap disagreed with its safe chain. A follow-up should verify this assumption by scanning historical production channel data.\n\n🤖 *Co-created with openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol*",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-13T09:10:32Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-08-21T19:02:59Z",
      "additions": 9,
      "deletions": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABAjf4Ig",
      "title": "interop: Align expiry-boundary restatements with the normative invariant",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 932,
      "body": "The message-expiry boundary is stated three times in the interop specs. The two summary restatements are one second stricter than the normative Message Expiry Invariant, which invalidates only `id.timestamp + EXPIRY_TIME < executing_block.timestamp` — so a message executed exactly at the boundary is valid.\n\nThis aligns both summaries with the normative text:\n\n- `messaging.md` invariants list: \"lower than\" becomes \"lower than or equal to\".\n- `derivation.md` invariants list: `t > execution_timestamp - expiry_window` becomes `>=`.\n\nBoth consensus implementations (op-supernode and kona) already accept the boundary case, so no implementation change is needed.\n\nFixes ethereum-optimism/specs#931",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T13:29:50Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-08-21T14:12:08Z",
      "additions": 3,
      "deletions": 2
    }
  ],
